    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>You learn to carry the body that cannot carry itself.</em></p><p>You may pick up an <strong>unconscious, bound, or Staggered creature</strong> of your size or smaller as a <strong>bonus action</strong>, without spending or reducing your remaining movement that turn (the L1 Soul speed penalty still applies only to the Soul Package, not to a creature you are physically carrying).</p><p>You may <strong>hand off</strong> a carried creature to an ally in an adjacent space as a <strong>free action</strong>. The hand-off does not provoke reactions.</p><p>You may <strong>carry a creature one size larger than yourself</strong> at half your movement speed, no Package penalty stacking — though the GM may adjudicate that this is conspicuous in tight terrain.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
